---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { SITE } from "../../consts";
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`About — ${SITE.author}`}
  description="From backend engineer to AEO engineer — how my search-and-data work in commerce and logistics carried over into the age of AI answer engines."
  locale="en"
  path="/about/"
  ogType="profile"
>
  <div class="prose prose-zinc max-w-none dark:prose-invert prose-headings:tracking-tight prose-a:text-accent">
    <h1>About</h1>

    <p>
      I'm Beomyong Choi — a backend engineer who moved into AI, now focused on Answer Engine
      Optimization (AEO).
    </p>

    <h2>A backend engineer who worked on search and data</h2>
    <p>
      I spent most of my career in the backend of large-scale services. I started at FinTalk, a
      fintech startup, building a matching service for financial advisors. Then I spent five-plus
      years at WeMakePrice, one of Korea's large e-commerce platforms.
    </p>
    <p>
      At WeMakePrice I worked deep on <strong>search and data</strong>: I built a system that
      automatically extracted the lowest-price product from catalogs, shipped product search, and
      ran crawler pipelines (AWS SQS) that collected thousands of records a day from shopping sites
      and influencer social feeds. I also handled traffic spikes of tens of thousands of concurrent
      users during real-time-search-keyword events.
    </p>
    <p>
      Later, at Hanexpress, I designed the shared modules and system architecture for logistics
      fulfillment solutions (WMS/FMS) and built an AWS EKS–based microservices platform end to end —
      which gave me a view of everything from application code to infra operations.
    </p>

    <h2>AI, and the next chapter of search</h2>
    <p>
      Watching LLMs change how search works pulled me toward AI. I completed AIFFEL's AI research
      track, went deep into NLP, and researched and built a RAG-based Q&amp;A system with my team.
    </p>
    <p>
      Now I focus on <strong>AEO (Answer Engine Optimization)</strong> — measuring and improving how
      brands show up inside AI answer engines like ChatGPT, Gemini, Claude, and Perplexity. I design
      measurement pipelines (LangGraph) that query multiple models at once, and I've applied them to
      real clients to move the numbers.
    </p>
    <p>
      Looking back, the search-and-data work I did in commerce carried straight over into AEO for
      the age of AI search.
    </p>

    <h2>Where I'm headed</h2>
    <p>
      I want to grow into an <strong>AI architect</strong> who designs scalable, cost-efficient AI
      systems — solving practical problems with a view of the whole system so AI services can grow
      reliably.
    </p>
    <p>
      For more, see my <a href="/en/resume/">resume</a> and <a href="/en/work/">work</a>, or reach
      out by <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>email</a> or <a href={SITE.linkedin}>LinkedIn</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
